The  pseudo‐device  simulates a 64‐bit wide device.  The state of
the simulated device can be manipulated  through  the  interface.
For  this  purpose,  access  the  "hw.gpiosim<N>.value" variable,
where "<N>" denotes the number of the instance.   Both  edge  and
level  interrupts are simulated.  The "hw.gpiosim<N>.ms" variable
will change the amount of time between ticks for simulated  level
interrupts.  The driver was written by Simulated interrupts added
